# XSH tcdrain()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Terminal tests use a pseudo-terminal (XSI). Output is made untransmittable by suspending
# it with tcflow(TCOOFF) and writing a byte; on a pseudo-terminal "transmitted" is taken to
# mean handed to the manager side. Background tests run in a session of their own with the
# pseudo-terminal as controlling terminal (implementation-defined acquisition: UNRESOLVED when
# it does not happen).

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.001
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       After a byte written to a pseudo-terminal subsidiary has been read
           from the manager, tcdrain() returns 0 (the call is bounded by an
           alarm).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/001-returns-zero.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.002
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       With output suspended and one byte written (so not transmitted),
           tcdrain() does not return; once output is restarted it returns 0 and
           the byte reaches the manager.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           Suspension is made with tcflow(TCOOFF); if the held byte reaches the
           manager anyway the test is UNRESOLVED.
timeout    40
test       t/002-blocks.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.003
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#ERRORS/EINTR
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       With output suspended and one byte written, tcdrain() waiting for the
           output is interrupted by a caught signal (no SA_RESTART) and returns
           -1 with EINTR.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           If the call does not block the test is UNRESOLVED.
timeout    40
test       t/003-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.004
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcdrain(-1) and tcdrain() of a closed descriptor return -1 with EBADF.
test       t/004-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.005
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcdrain() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe and
           /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/005-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.006
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group (not orphaned) whose SIGTTOU
           is neither blocked nor ignored and which calls tcdrain() on its
           controlling terminal is sent SIGTTOU (default action: stopped).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/006-bg-sigttou.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.007
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group which calls tcdrain() on its
           controlling terminal while SIGTTOU is blocked, and again while it is
           ignored, completes normally (returns 0), is not stopped.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    60
test       t/007-bg-quiet.c

assertion  XSH.tcdrain.008
anchor     functions/tcdrain.html#ERRORS/EIO
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in an orphaned process group, with SIGTTOU neither blocked
           nor ignored, which calls tcdrain() on its controlling terminal gets -1
           with EIO.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/008-orphan-eio.c
